// Moves for B10, the Bellwright (registry 39100-39119). Source:
// docs/game/05-enemies-and-bosses.md, "B10 The Bellwright": a hammer giant who hauls a frozen bell
// on a chain. The fight runs on a beat (one every 40 ticks, 32 in phase 2) and every attack here
// lands on one. Hit and frame numbers are tuning, set by that grid (lf_core::ai::bosses::b10):
//   - The Bellwright only picks a move 9 ticks after a beat (the "slot"), so a move starts at
//     beat + 9 and its first hit lands on the next beat: frame 32 in phase 1, frame 24 in phase 2
//     (a hit on frame F lands F - 1 ticks after the pick; a 32- or 24-tick telegraph: the hammer
//     or flail goes up, the bell rocks on its chain).
//   - Later hits come one beat apart (40 or 32 frames), and every move's `total_frames` is a
//     whole number of beats, so the next slot is always on the grid.
//   - Phase 1 moves are 80, 120, 120, and 160 frames; phase 2 moves are 64, 96, and 128.
// Every combo ends in a punish window of at least 20 ticks (36 or more here; checked by
// `lf_content::boss::check`). The toll's shockwave is not a move: it is `b10`'s mechanic.
// Damage comes from the body's `attack`, so `motion_value` is the only multiplier.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
[
  (
    // Overhead hammer, one beat: the hammer rises for 32 ticks and the bell rocks back on its chain; it lands on the next beat. Ends in a 44-tick punish window.
    id: "b10_hammer",
